# Binaries
# Anchored to the repo root. An unanchored `ozymandis` matches at every depth and
# silently excludes cmd/ozymandis/, so a fresh clone has no main package to build.
/bin/
/dist/
/ozymandis
/oz
/docs/

# Go
# Keep coverage output anchored to the repository root.
*.test
*.out
/coverage.*

# templ generated files are committed so `go build` works without the templ CLI.
# If you prefer generating in CI instead, uncomment:
# *_templ.go

# Local config / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.kubeconfig
kubeconfig

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp

# Knowledge graph output. Regenerate with `/graphify` rather than committing it;
# graph.json and the HTML are large and change on every build.
/graphify-out/

# Authoring-time only. The built bundle in internal/web/assets/js is committed,
# so building and running Ozymandis need neither Node nor these.
/node_modules/
